#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084061} :activity/id #uuid "da88a97d-6c4e-5299-b921-71200664bd9d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049474 :topic/id #uuid "f80da52a-4a96-5269-8885-c600a798d61e" :topic/math-academy-id 790} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084061 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084526 :tutorial/content "Let's plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\n. According to the algebraic definition of absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n{x\\begin{vmatrix}forx \\ge 0 \\\\ -x\\end{vmatrix}forx < 0\n$$\n\nSo, the left-hand branch of the graph is the function $y=-x$, and the right-hand branch is $y=x$:\n\n![](images/60/60ad4dfdb6086f20f5137c5b4ac4905e55d5697ec4cf31575bf79be5fd408e0c.png)\n\nNotice that the graph has a sharp corner at $(0,0)$. We call this point the **vertex** or the **minimum point.**\n\nWe can apply **horizontal** and **vertical translations** to the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\n.\n\n- The graph of $y= \\mid x \\mid +a$ is a **vertical translation** of the absolute value graph $y= \\mid x \\mid$. It moves the graph $a$ units up.![](images/bc/bc56f0d75b8359f71a104580902a18a1d8009091b94694beb7f8ac71c9bfc9bc.png)\n- The graph of $y= \\mid x-a \\mid$ is a **horizontal translation** of the absolute value graph $y= \\mid x \\mid$. It moves the graph $a$ units to the *right*.![](images/1f/1f79063f7350e734811366545507fc44c321882d2d9b228b85475a27d46c1759.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When drawing horizontal and vertical translations, it is easiest to transform the graph's vertex first. Then, the two branches can be drawn coming out of the vertex.\n- When we translate the graph $y= \\mid x \\mid$, the resulting curve is called the **image** of $y = \\mid x \\mid$ under the translation." :tutorial/id #uuid "1b8dce6a-8742-581b-80f6-e39c9943b395" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9295 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "bdb8f706-56c3-508a-a745-c4cf4b268e01" :step/math-academy-id 169443 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084062}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084062 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083189 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082947 :question/id #uuid "5a2db9be-6ef3-5466-a7cc-4e7e2b5670ec" :question/math-academy-id "e-14919"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61ec00a6-06ae-5d78-bb1a-b06351432cc3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049534} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049844}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083554} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083623}] :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Vertical Translation"} :step/id #uuid "6d0878f5-845c-5163-b1ae-e72f37806b6d" :step/math-academy-id 169444 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084063}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084063 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083190 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082948 :question/id #uuid "2e688f8d-16cc-58d6-8791-538cc335ce04" :question/math-academy-id "e-14925"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "05cffafa-cfcf-5979-a413-b7d0b66dd434" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083676}] :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Horizontal Translation"} :step/id #uuid "dfd03723-b5ce-5ca8-98bb-2b1cf56700d6" :step/math-academy-id 169447 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084064}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084064 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084528 :tutorial/content "Horizontal and vertical translations can be combined. It does not matter which we do first.\n\nIn general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-h \\mid +k\n$$\n\nis a translation of the graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n- $k$ units up." :tutorial/id #uuid "b55739df-8b0d-5ef2-9702-d56de0246597" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9302 :tutorial/title "Combining Translations"} :step/id #uuid "3287422a-9367-5f91-9957-0152a7e772df" :step/math-academy-id 169450 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084065}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084065 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083191 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082949 :question/id #uuid "82de263c-391b-5d45-bbd6-353c31c806fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-14933"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca5dcf12-db1a-5cfc-b369-986caa8f666c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083625} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083628}] :knowledge-point/title "Combining Horizontal and Vertical Translations"} :step/id #uuid "09be9587-52a8-510c-841a-fe31ae2eb30e" :step/math-academy-id 169451}] :activity/title "Absolute Value Graphs" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186083468}]}
